id: pm-gh1073
title: "GH-1073: pm init accepts a whitespace id prefix that makes later creates fail"
description: "GitHub issue #1073 reports that init persists a natural-language prefix containing spaces, then every later create fails the stricter normalized-ID contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:init",github,validation
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:41:56.036Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:49.680Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:49.080Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:49.080Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Share one prefix validation primitive between SDK init and lifecycle create; fail before tracker persistence or normalize deterministically; cover CLI/SDK/MCP and packed npx/bunx behavior; document accepted prefix grammar and recovery.
parent: pm-7t04
severity: high
repro_steps: "Initialize a fresh tracker with a whitespace-containing prefix, then create an item with or without an explicit ID; observe the downstream normalization refusal."
resolution: "Resolved: init canonicalizes natural-language ID prefixes through the shared SDK contract before settings persistence and item creation."
expected_result: "Init normalizes or rejects an invalid prefix before committing tracker state, using the same actionable ID contract as create."
actual_result: Init succeeds and persists a prefix that makes ordinary item creation fail.
affected_version: 2026.8.20
component: tracker initialization
